B.avO=new A.rh(0,"kalimas")
B.at7=new A.l2(1,"Allah is One","\u0627\u0644\u062a\u0648\u062d\u064a\u062f","Islam begins with one sentence. None has the right to be worshipped except Allah, and Muhammad is His Messenger. Worship means the prayer, the sacrifice, the vow, and the call for help. All of that is for Allah alone. Read the first two kalimas aloud until the meaning is as clear as the Arabic.","Recite the shahada slowly, then explain it in your own words to someone in the house.","Open the kalimas",B.avO)
B.avP=new A.rh(1,"wudu")
B.ata=new A.l2(2,"Become ready to pray","\u0627\u0644\u0648\u0636\u0648\u0621","Salah is not valid without purity. Wudu is washing the face, the arms to the elbows, wiping the head, and washing the feet to the ankles. The Prophet \ufdfa also washed his hands, rinsed his mouth, and rinsed his nose. Water must reach the skin. A wipe over a dry spot does not count.","Make wudu once with the guide open, then once from memory.","Open the wudu guide",B.avP)
B.avQ=new A.rh(2,"salah")
B.atd=new A.l2(3,"The five prayers","\u0627\u0644\u0635\u0644\u0627\u0629","The five prayers are Fajr, Dhuhr, Asr, Maghrib, and Isha. Each rak'ah has standing with Al-Fatiha, bowing, two prostrations, and sitting. Fajr is two rak'ahs, Dhuhr and Asr are four, Maghrib is three, and Isha is four. Pray them on time. A prayer made at the edge of its time is still owed, and making it up is better than leaving it.","Pray the next salah using the guide if you are still learning the positions.","Open the prayer guide",B.avQ)
B.avR=new A.rh(3,"fatiha")
B.at8=new A.l2(4,"The surah of every prayer","\u0627\u0644\u0641\u0627\u062a\u062d\u0629","Al-Fatiha is required in every rak'ah. It praises Allah, asks Him alone for help, and asks for the straight path. Learn one ayah at a time. Hide the Arabic and say it back. When all seven stay in your memory, recite them in the next prayer without looking.","Mark every line of Al-Fatiha in Memorize, then pray one rak'ah with it from memory.","Practice Al-Fatiha",B.avR)
B.avS=new A.rh(4,"adhkar")
B.atb=new A.l2(5,"Remember Allah at the edges of the day","\u0627\u0644\u0623\u0630\u0643\u0627\u0631","The morning and evening adhkar are short phrases the Prophet \ufdfa repeated: glory to Allah, praise to Allah, Allah is the greatest, and seeking refuge with the last two surahs. They are not a replacement for the prayer. They keep the tongue busy with something that benefits it.","Read the morning set once after Fajr, or the evening set after Asr.","Open the morning adhkar",B.avS)
B.avT=new A.rh(5,"seerah")
B.at9=new A.l2(6,"How he lived","\u0627\u0644\u0633\u064a\u0631\u0629","The Prophet \ufdfa was born in Makkah, received the Quran at forty, was patient through the boycott and the Year of Sorrow, migrated to Madinah, and returned to Makkah as a forgiver. His character is part of the message. A person can memorize rules and still miss the way he treated his family, the poor, and people who harmed him.","Read three events on the seerah timeline and tell one of them to someone else.","Open the seerah",B.avT)
B.avU=new A.rh(6,"zakat")
B.atc=new A.l2(7,"Wealth has a right in it","\u0627\u0644\u0632\u0643\u0627\u0629","When savings reach the nisab and a lunar year passes, zakat is 2.5 percent. It is a pillar, not a tip. Below the nisab, voluntary charity is still open: food, a kind word, and removing something harmful from a path are all sadaqah. The point of this day is to know whether zakat is currently due, and to give something either way.","Run your numbers in the zakat calculator, then give any amount of sadaqah today.","Open the zakat calculator",B.avU)
